ing along in the social world is to  not let people know when they when  they've upset you to not let them know  if they've hurt your feelings to not let  them know if they've made you angry to  not and very often  to not let them know if uh if they've  turned you on if they've you know made  you feel excited in their presence  so  and actors get to do that they they get  to they get to express things that are  very human things that  um  that in real life are are frowned upon  you know the social parameters are very  strict  often  so the notion that acting is lying where  do you think that came from  from people who don't know anything  about acting well I think if you don't  know anything about how what acting is  about is really about the subtext  then it's easy to think that it's it  it's not that people are stupid for  thinking that because an actor is  pretending to be in love with somebody  when they're married to somebody else or  they're you know they're they're  pretending to uh murder somebody  uh when they're when they claim that  they're an upstanding citizen so  um  I could see where where it comes from  that it you know that it has to do with  uh that people would think that  but it's unfortunate  um it it has to do with not  understanding this idea of subtext that  that an actor can be completely truthful  with their own subtext and an actor  never needs to let go of their own  values or their own uh yeah their own  values their own ethics  an actor never needs to let go of those  and and I don't know I like to keep  telling people about that that that uh  you know an actor can be capable of  approaching every character without  judgment very important for an actor not  to judge their character to to be on  their character's side to look for the  ways that the character is  doing what they think is best is doing  the best they can  but without and to understand that as a  craft  and it doesn't mean that you have to let  go of your own ethics sure but you could  say that we all have certain parts of  every character in us whether we act  exactly exactly we all have impulses we  all have we all have every impulse every  single person has every single impulse  in them somewhere now for some people  they're buried so far down that they  won't wouldn't recognize it in  themselves for actors they allow those  things to be buried less far down you  know so that they can access them but it  doesn't mean that they change their  beliefs about what's right and wrong
 

